Rule 14. Every action is classified as "breaks_no_law", unless either that action is classified as "breaks_first_law" or that action is classified as "breaks_zeroth_law", or both.
Rule 15. Every action is classified as "candidate_action", if that action is classified as "breaks_no_law".
Rule 16. Every action is classified as "candidate_action", if it is not the case that there is a robot such that both that action is available to that robot and that robot is classified as "has_lawful_option", unless that action is classified as "breaks_zeroth_law".
Rule 17. Every action is classified as "possibly_harmful", if there is a harm such that both that harm is classified as "harms_human" and that action might lead to that harm.
Rule 18 (exception to rule 9). Every action must not be performed, if both that action is classified as "possibly_harmful" and that action is classified as "beaten_by_a_candidate".
Rule 19 (exception to rule 8). Every action may be performed, if that action is classified as "candidate_action", unless either that action is classified as "beaten_by_a_candidate" or that action is classified as "breaks_zeroth_law", or both.
Rule 20. Every action is classified as "valid_order", if both that action is classified as "ordered" and that action is classified as "breaks_no_law", unless both that action is classified as "possibly_harmful" and that action is classified as "beaten_by_a_candidate".
Rule 21. Every first action has the recorded relation "prevails_over" to each second action, if both the first action has the recorded relation "competes_with" to the second action and the first action has the recorded relation "outranks" to the second action.
Rule 22. Every first action has the recorded relation "prevails_over" to each second action, if both the first action has the recorded relation "competes_with" to the second action and the first action has the recorded relation "ordered_before" to the second action, unless the second action has the recorded relation "outranks" to the first action.
Rule 23. Every action is classified as "overridden_order", if there is a second action such that both the second action is classified as "valid_order" and the second action has the recorded relation "prevails_over" to that action.
Rule 24 (exception to rule 11). Every action need not be performed, if that action is classified as "overridden_order".
Rule 25. Every action is classified as "possibly_harmful", if there is a harm such that both that action has the recorded relation "own_robot_harm" to that harm and that action might lead to that harm, unless that action is classified as "ordered".
Rule 26. Every action has the recorded relation "own_robot_harm" to each harm, if there is a robot such that both that action is available to that robot and that harm has the recorded relation "harm_to" to that robot.
Rule 27. Every first action has the recorded relation "competes_with" to each second action, if there is a robot such that both the first action is available to that robot and the second action is available to that robot.
Rule 28. Every first action has the recorded relation "less_severe_competitor" to each second action, if both the first action has the recorded relation "competes_with" to the second action and the first action has a less severe worst case than the second action.
Rule 29. Every action is classified as "beaten_by_a_candidate", if there is a second action such that both the second action is classified as "candidate_action" and the second action has the recorded relation "less_severe_competitor" to that action.
